  "overview": "**BLiP** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#00c6d7` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Nunito Sans` (54px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `#ffffff` -> `rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)` surface layering.\n\nSource: published token package (https://github.com/takenet/blip-ds), repo https://github.com/takenet/blip-ds, package `blip-ds`, frameworks: web-components, react. Inventory: **91** colors, **8** typography steps, and **16** documented components (see repository license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 16 component tokens with documented paddings: `10px 18px`, `9px 13px`, `18px 20px`, `4px 10px`, `10px 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#ffffff` -> `rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#00c6d7` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#00c6d7` with `#0b0b0c` text (9.4:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Nunito Sans` headings with `Nunito Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (12px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `rgba(255, 255, 255, 1)` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-default` fields and secondary buttons."
}
